    "Scouting Notes": "Displays some pop from both sides, though I like him a lot more as a left handed hitter.\n Solid defender, looks better at second base than short. \n Known for his ultra aggressive swings, may try to go with more of a bat to ball approach in pro ball.\n Gamer mentality. Consistently trying to take an extra base. So far in pro ball, it has not been working out super well but I like the aggressiveness.\n Above average runner, should be a double digit base stealer pretty easily.\n This is a young draft eligible college player who had a much better sophomore year than junior year.\n There is some upside to the pick and came in under slot which helped them land Misiorowski (saved $115,000).",
